  "cover_text": "A fairly cold last half of January meant that I could not host that lovely postcard photograph. Instead, I followed the beautiful path of light through the three jonitions so elegantly photographed in the twilight of 1934 by Elinor Wildwick-Miller.\nDistinctive sets of canal- and green lawn fence walls stretch up from the shoreline into the glistening underwater world of family passers-by, of watching children's experiments be carried out in the faraway land areas of a quiet fishing village. Couple of nuns here and there believe it",
